{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794995971","published":"2026-11-18T09:59:47Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:30.677129716Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116303","CVE-2026-116308","CVE-2026-116311","CVE-2026-116321","CVE-2026-116327","CVE-2026-120146","CVE-2026-120154","CVE-2026-16237","CVE-2026-16240"],"summary":"postgresql: Fix of 9 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-120154: check the ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE target row against RLS\n  policies before evaluating the user-supplied WHERE clause\n- CVE-2026-16237: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE through an automatically\n  updatable view now fails when the conflicting row is not visible through the\n  view\n- CVE-2026-116311: DROP OWNED BY no longer changes row-level security policies\n  on tables the current user does not own\n- CVE-2026-116327: treat a leaky function applied to a CaseTestExpr or Param as\n  leaky, so it is not evaluated before row-level security quals\n- CVE-2026-120146: REASSIGN OWNED requires the CREATEDB privilege to change the\n  owner of a database, as ALTER DATABASE ... OWNER TO does\n- CVE-2026-116308: dict_int: return NULL for a zero-length token instead of\n  reading past its end\n- CVE-2026-116321: prevent construction of invalid \"name\" values via array\n  element assignment\n- CVE-2026-16240: pg_basebackup: do not use received backup manifest data as a\n  format string\n- CVE-2026-116303: check EXECUTE privilege on the cast functions used by foreign\n  key checks and by to_json()/to_jsonb()","affected":[{"package":{"name":"postgresql","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/postgresql?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"13.23-1.el9_6.tuxcare.els20"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1794995971.json"}},{"package":{"name":"postgresql-contrib","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/postgresql-contrib?distro=almali